# opencode

The server is registered globally in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` as
`bismut-vector`.

## What was added

```json
"mcp": {
    "bismut-vector": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
            "C:/Program Files/nodejs/node.exe",
            "/path/to/Bismut_MCP_Vector/dist/index.js"
        ],
        "enabled": true,
        "environment": {
            "BISMUT_DB_PATH": "/path/to/Bismut_MCP_Vector/.bismut/vectors.db",
            "BISMUT_CACHE_DIR": "/path/to/Bismut_MCP_Vector/.bismut/cache",
            "BISMUT_LOG_LEVEL": "warn"
        }
    }
}
```

## Why these values

- `node.exe` is absolute so the server does not depend on `PATH`.
- Paths are absolute so the entry works no matter which directory opencode was
  started from.
- `BISMUT_DB_PATH` is explicit for the same reason: the database must not move
  when the working directory changes.
- `BISMUT_LOG_LEVEL` is `warn` so ordinary startup chatter stays out of the
  session while real problems remain visible.

## Verifying

`scripts/verify-opencode-config.mjs` reads the live opencode config, iterates
every registered server, and performs a real MCP handshake with the exact
command and environment values it finds there.

```powershell
npm run verify:opencode                        # uses the current directory
npm run verify:opencode -- /path/to/some-project
```

Pass a path to check how the server behaves inside a specific project.

## Per-project overrides

Project config deep-merges over global, so list only what differs:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "bismut-vector": {
      "environment": { "BISMUT_COLLECTION": "myproject" }
    }
  }
}
```

Setting a distinct `BISMUT_COLLECTION` per project keeps corpora separate.

To disable the server for one project:

```json
{ "mcp": { "bismut-vector": { "enabled": false } } }
```

## Verifying in a session

Ask opencode what tools it has, or go straight to work:

> Index this repository with index_paths, then search it for how player input
> is handled.

The first `index_paths` call is slow because it downloads the embedding model
(~120 MB) into `.bismut/cache`. Later calls are fast.

## Removing

Delete the `mcp` block from `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`. The database
and model cache under `.bismut/` can be deleted independently.